S[101] = "6.1 Interpreting the Solow residual"
S[102] = ("Under M0, any error in the timing or composition of capital passes into TFP. Our results show that, under stated assumptions, part of measured TFP levels and growth variation can be reassigned to two accounting parameters, ⟦μ(t)⟧ and ⟦β⟧. This does not imply that innovation is unimportant; it implies that residual interpretation should follow, not precede, an audit of capital conventions. The boundary between mis-timed accounting and genuine change is itself porous: if gestation lengthens because assets require software integration, regulatory approval or network complementarities, the correction also describes an economic change in the composition of capital.")
